i have seen way too many bias sponsored  reviews on this msi creator z16 so today  let's get honest and talk about the good  and the bad and if this is the ultimate  16-inch laptop for creatives like myself  and many of you guys but first i need to  give a thank you to microcenter for  sending this over for review micro  center has 25 stores nationwide with an  impressive variety of electronics from  gaming vr computer parts like processors  graphics and everything else needed to  build a pc they also have a huge variety  of desktops laptops and all the  accessories that you need not only that  but also highly trained staff and low  prices or use the link down below to  view the creator z16 at microcenter.com  they are also giving away a free 240  gigabyte ssd to new customers get all  the info in the link in the video  description right out of the gate i was  interested in this laptop because of the  intel 11th generation 45 watt rated  processor that is based on a 10  nanometer design we've been waiting for  these ships since 2016 2017 or so and we  finally have them so i want to see how  well they perform but as far as the  laptop itself i wasn't expecting that  much i actually had my very first laptop  for creative purposes photo editing  video editing was an msi and it was a  great bang for the buck laptop but it  did have a lot of flaws with this thing  i was surprised right away when i took  it out of the box because of how well  built it is now the older ones were  aluminum but they were very thin  aluminum where this thing is super solid  there's no chassis flex  even if you open this thing up it is  super sturdy now with that it is a  little bit on the heavier side you're  looking at about five pounds compared to  you know four or four and a half so that  is noticeable but i would definitely  take that  because of the extra durability just how  well it is designed now everything else  is nice about it the keyboard it feels  great i have no complaints trackpad  accurate smooth it is a diving board  design so if you're clicking above the  halfway point it is tougher to click i  ended up just tapping for that and one  very interesting thing with it is not  only do we have a fingerprint scanner  that is not built into the power button  for some reason but with that we also  have windows hello which i absolutely  love so not a lot of laptops offer you  both options now another thing that  surprised me is the fact the display  lays down pretty much flat uh maybe even  a little bit more than that now taking a  look at the bottom and the sides we see  a ton of vents which this laptop really  needs along with speakers at the bottom  which we'll also talk about that is a  nice positive and then on the sides we  have a big variety of ports we have two  thunderbolt 4 ports two usb a's which is  nice to have even if this thing is  pretty thin and they are the full speed  10 gigabit per second not the five and  then we also have a micro sd card slot  now this is interesting because this is  a uhs three and i don't even know if we  have uhs three cards yet but it is gonna  be future proof uh personally though i  wish it was a full-size sd card you can  always get an adapter for the micros but  you can't go larger so i don't really  know what they were thinking as far as  putting that in there and then as far as  power we do have a full-size barrel plug  because this thing does need a good  amount of power now back to the speakers  i have to say that these are the best  speakers i've ever heard in a windows  laptop there are four separate drivers  they get loud they have good bass i was  honestly shocked by how well they  sounded my previous msi sounded terrible  it was bad and many laptops like the  dells and say the razers they've gotten  a little better but they still sound bad  but this thing  was awesome let's go ahead and see how  it compares to the 16-inch macbook pro  that has the best speakers in any laptop  by far  [Music]  [Music]  all right guys let me know your thoughts  down in the comment section below it is  actually louder if you have it placed on  top of a desk because they do fire down  and then bounce up and if there's not a  ton of frequencies it actually could  sound better like with  instrumental stuff like that with just  voices once you have a lot of different  sounds it does fall behind the macbook  pros and that has six speakers that are  well tuned but overall man i was really  really impressed now as far as the  cameras and the microphones we have a  720p webcam it looks okay you clearly  see the person there are a lot of  compression artifacts to denoise it  but it's about average now the  microphones on the other hand they don't  have a lot of bass pickup but they are  very clear so the people on the other  side will be able to understand what  you're saying now before we get into the  performance and my biggest complaint  let's talk about a couple more positives  the first one being the ssd i'm glad i  tested it out because it is a pcr  express 4 and it runs super fast we have  read speeds of 5 500 and around 4 300  write speeds the performance is  incredible and this is gonna make a  difference when we start talking about  real world performance and the next  thing that really surprised me was the  display and msi talks a lot about it on  the website and now i can see why it is  awesome right between 4k and 1080p  that's great for battery life and also  for windows scaling  not only that but each one is factory  calibrated so the colors looked pretty  much identical to my macbook pro the  closest i have seen it gets nice and  bright reflectivity is a little bit  higher than macbook pro but not bad  and with that it supports dci p3 colors  so the colors look awesome great for  color grading and on top of that what's  something that my mac pro can do is the  display is a 120 hertz panel so  refresher is great nice and smooth and  then if you want to do some gaming with  that rtx graphics card you'll be able to  enjoy the higher refresh rates so good  job msi you killed it with this display  now inside of this machine is the tiger  lake 11th generation a 10 nanometer  processor this is the i7 8 cores going  up to 4.6 gigahertz so finally we have  that chip so how well does it do well  i'll overall let you guys know it's  pretty good i was pretty surprised and  in speedometer 2.0 browser benchmark it  scored pretty much 190 that is the  highest i have seen in any machine other  than the m1 macbook pros which  absolutely kill it in this so as far as  snappiness it is amazing and that makes  sense because this chip it literally  scales up its wattage and frequency all  the time it wants to maximize  performance and so i see it ramping up  all the time which we'll talk about but  as far as geekbench the performance is  also really good we have a single core  of 1400 and a multi-core of 7  800. now that is really impressive it's  great job beating out the m1 by a little  bit there but what i was interested in  is will this machine still be able to  perform that well  when you unplug it a lot of machines  slow down now this one did slow down but  not by that much by about 12 13  as far as the cpu so that is definitely  acceptable when you're not feeding it uh  power now of course macbooks they don't  slow down but i've seen some machines  that go down like 50 in power it is  terrible now when you're maxing out the  cpus like in cinebench i got a score of  10  300 that is about 20 percent better than  the 16-inch macbook pro that has an 8  core i9 processor remember this is the  i7 uh the i9 would get a little bit more  than this but not much because of  thermal throttling but that still is a  great improvement going down to 10  nanometers now with that we also hit 55  watts of power usage it actually doesn't  let it spike up higher to like say 60 70  like on a macbook so it is limiting it  but it does hit that really quickly  along with really high temperatures  almost instantly it ends up heating up  to 96 97 degrees so this 1080 nanometer  isn't really helping that much that's  because intel just is trying to get as  much performance as they can they have a  lot of competition with amd and with  apple as far as graphics this thing has  an rtx 3060 built in with six gigabytes  of video memory now first i thought it's  going to be limiting i thought maybe  they should have put in something better  but after testing it out i think it's  actually a really nice balance and other  laptops have other limitations as well  and the performance is pretty dang good  now as far as the cuda performance in  geekbench it got a really high 94 000.  that is a killer score so this graphics  are performing well but once again how  well does it perform when you unplug it  i've seen some go from 100 000 or more  down to 35 but thankfully msi is not  limiting it much and it actually got a  score of 83 000 so once again it's about  12 13 of a performance drop which is  definitely acceptable and you're going  to get most of your performance when  you're on battery power now what does  all of this mean in the real world well  as far as photo editing i have to say  that other than my mac pro i have not  seen anything go this fast and that mac  pro is about 15 grand switching through  photos was super quick very snappy  faster than the m1 and the same thing  with using brushes very very quick now i  think that's because one that ssd is  extremely fast and then two um it has  really good performance with the acre  processor and it's scaling up all the  time now one thing that was annoying is  even when i'm just switching photos the  fans are constantly spinning up  constantly spinning up and even  sometimes during web browsing and so  with this good performance i was like  maybe i should just slow it down a  little bit so i lowered the performance  setting in windows but didn't matter it  still kept running at really high  performance but also having those  annoying fans now as far as exporting  our standard 50 raw image test this  thing did it in a minute and 59 seconds  it is incredibly fast this laptop is  just great for photo editing now what  about on the other side for video  editing well i started playing back some  h.265 footage with some effects some  luts film grain and it had no issues  whatsoever now not only that only about  18  of the graphics card was being utilized  so there's tons of overhead so after  dealing some video editing i saw that  this gpu is more than good enough unless  you're doing like 8k footage or crazy  multi-camera raw stuff i don't think you  need a 30-70 or a 80. now when i  exported this project i was also quite  surprised it took a minute and 54  seconds to export my five minute project  so once again super quick beating out  the previous macbook pro 16 inch still a  bit slower than the new m1 with the  update but that is incredible for a five  minute project now overall i have a lot  of good things to say other than the fan  noise and realistically i don't know  what you could do you could slow it down  and i probably would slow it down but  then you start losing the benefits of  intel 11 gen and all the extra  performance and smoothness that you get  you'll kind of go back to a previous  processor if you don't want to deal with  the fan noise and the heat and of course  with that high wattage and with those  high boost clocks it just keeps coming  out so like half the time when i'm using  this the fan is kicking up and down and  to me that is just really really  annoying um but a lot of windows do  laptops do that you know especially if  you're trying to push them to the limit  so if you're okay with that  how does this compare to the competition  well with the dell you do get an oled  screen for the same price point or  slightly more but the graphics card is a  lot weaker  so because of that and because this is a  120 hertz screen that is calibrated and  great and overall it's a good package i  would recommend it if you're looking for  a windows laptop with a screen to size  as long as you're either going to tweak  the fans or maybe you know not care  about that so once again thank you for  micro center for sending it over if you  guys want to see us compare it to say a  16 inch macro pro or an m1 how that  competes with the 11th gen let us know  and click that subscribe button above  and check out one of those great videos  right over there that's been max and  i'll see you in the next video  [Music]

